Kernel 1.2 — the-cave (First Production Spec)

This is your first buildable artifact.

1. Purpose

Prove that:

one participant can present (tell a story)
another can perceive the same focal element
and respond in real time

This establishes:

shared perception + directed attention + exchange

2. Venue
Name

the-cave

Capacity Target
~2–100 participants (soft target)
includes all roles
Geometry (v1)

Simplified implementation:

Flat ground plane
Backdrop wall (mountain-like visual)
Fire element at center-front
No terrain editing
No vertical complexity
3. Zones
Stage
centered on fire
visible to all
actor performs here
Audience Area
facing stage
default camera/view origin
receives performance + reactions
Backstage
hidden from audience
conceptually exists (may be UI-layer first, not 3D yet)
Interface Layer (Overlay)
banners above fire
minimal UI elements
reaction indicators
4. Roles
Director
full visibility
controls reveal/hide
controls segmentation (future)
sees all reactions (except producer-private)
Actor (Cast)
performs
can speak
can create elements (configurable)
sees stage + audience (+ limited backstage)
Audience
sees stage
can react
can send note cards
no direct stage manipulation
Producer
initially inherits director or privileged audience view
full authority not fully exposed in UI yet
5. Core Elements
Required (v1)
Fire
type: image (static)
position: stage center
Text (speech display)
appears near speaker or as overlay
Reaction tokens
visual/emotional indicators
Note cards
routed messages
