10. Time Model
system progresses through moments
actions occur within moments
no retroactive contradiction of past
new actions append forward
11. Element Lifecycle

States:

session (default)
production (optional)
library (producer-approved)
Rules
actors may create elements (configurable)
producer controls persistence into library
constraints:
file type
size
format
12. Exchange Model (Critical)
Outbound
actor speaks
fire is visible
Inbound
audience reacts
audience sends note cards

This must work in real time.

13. Non-Goals (v1)

Explicitly NOT included:

terrain editing
underground systems
cameras/broadcast scaling
black box modular stage
LMS features (grades, records, etc.)
marketplace
complex segmentation logic
full chat systems
advanced UI panels
14. Success Criteria

The system is successful when:

Two users connect
One is actor, one is audience
Both see the same fire
Actor sends a message (“Once, by this fire…”)
Audience perceives it
Audience reacts (e.g., clap)
Actor/director can perceive that reaction

If that works:

the system lives